# verify-routing-register.yaml -- declared tier anchors for every verify-leg routing
# surface (backlog v3.0-77; the router-side backstop for the 2026-07-29 tier-promotion
# incident). check-substrate.py's anti-promotion pin protects the POLICY
# (substrate_gate_ok); the pickler instance's promotion never touched the policy -- it
# edited the ROUTING (driver dispatch, backend passthrough, bridge direction) so a
# routine leg could only ever reach a vendor-pinned verifier. These rows declare, per
# routing surface, the one short semantic source line that EMBODIES its tier declaration;
# deploy/check-verify-routing.py asserts each marker is still present. A missing marker
# is a BLOCKING finding: either the tier declaration was edited (the promotion class --
# revert it) or a legitimate refactor moved it (update the row IN THE SAME commit, citing
# the decision that authorized the change). Raising a leg's tier is a decision, not a fix.
#
# Honest residual (recorded, not hidden): marker presence catches edits TO the declared
# tier lines -- the incident's exact shape -- not every conceivable routing rewrite
# around them. The runtime backstop stays check-substrate.py (policy pin, 23/23) and the
# journaled substrate blocks (F17/F18) on every leg.
#
# Row schema: id, file, marker (exact substring, one line), means, decision-ref.

rows:
  - id: driver-routine-dispatch
    file: deploy/compile-driver.py
    marker: 'gate_kind="routine"'
    means: the ordinary wired-compile verify leg dispatches at ROUTINE tier (model_id separation suffices)
    decision-ref: v3.0-65 build spec; v3.0-76 (tier doctrine)
  - id: backends-gate-passthrough
    file: deploy/compile-backends.py
    marker: "self.gate_kind"
    means: the backend passes its CONSTRUCTED gate kind through to substrate_gate_ok -- never a hardcoded stricter literal
    decision-ref: v3.0-65 build spec
  - id: substrate-routine-branch
    file: deploy/check-substrate.py
    marker: "return absorb_model != verify_model"
    means: ROUTINE tier is model_id difference, same-vendor compliant
    decision-ref: v3.0-76 (anti-promotion pin guards this branch's semantics)
  - id: substrate-firewall-branch
    file: deploy/check-substrate.py
    marker: "return absorb_vendor != verify_vendor"
    means: MIGRATION/DESIGN tiers require vendor difference (the cross-substrate firewall stays intact -- de-promotion is watched too)
    decision-ref: v3.0-76
  - id: bridge-direction-doc
    file: .claude/skills/bridge/verify-cli.js
    marker: "routes to an OpenAI Codex/GPT verifier"
    means: the Claude-side bridge's declared direction; a vendor-pin rewrite of the bridge (the pickler edit's surface) removes or contradicts this line
    decision-ref: v3.0-77
